    intro="Technical debt in Scrum is the extra work a team creates for its future Sprints when it chooses a quick solution today instead of a better one that would take longer. Scrum handles it through transparency: you make debt visible in the Product Backlog, stop new debt with a strong Definition of Done, and pay existing debt down a little every Sprint. This guide shows you how to spot it, who decides when to fix it, and a step-by-step process with templates and a worked example.",
