          H3("How much Sprint capacity should go on technical debt?"),
          "There is no rule in the Scrum Guide and no agreed industry standard. Many teams start by reserving a modest share of capacity, often somewhere between 10% and 20%, and adjust it based on the trend in their warning signs. If cycle time and defects are improving, the share is working. If they are getting worse, raise it for a few Sprints, or move a specific high-interest item up the backlog. Make the decision at Sprint Planning with the Product Owner, using [capacity planning](/project-management/agile/agile-capacity-planning/) so the debt work is visible rather than hidden inside feature estimates.",
